key_passage.text:
Assuming a pinhole camera and using the depth, $z \left[n,m \right]$, and the intrinsic camera parameters, $\mathbf{K}$, we obtain the 3D coordinates for a pixel with image coordinates $[n,m]$ in the camera reference frame as $$\begin{aligned}
\begin{bmatrix}
X \\
Y \\ Z \end{bmatrix}
= z\left[n,m \right] \times \mathbf{K}^{-1} \times
\begin{bmatrix}
n \\
m \\ 1 \end{bmatrix}
\end{aligned}$$

